IMPORT prelude

-- Social Security Act -- the figures set each year, as a dated table.
--
-- The Act fixes formulas, not numbers: the Commissioner of Social Security determines and publishes in the Federal Register,
-- on or before 1 November each year, the PIA bend points (s 415(a)(1)(D)), the amount for a quarter of coverage
-- (s 413(d)(2)), the retirement earnings test exempt amounts (s 403(f)(8)(A)), the contribution and benefit base (s 430) and
-- the cost-of-living increase (s 415(i)), which also raises the SSI federal benefit rate (s 1382f). The Secretary promulgates
-- the Part B premium each September (s 1395r(a)(3)).
--
-- Only calendar year 2026 is deposited:
--   fr-2025-19763-ssa-cola-2026.txt   SSA, "Cost-of-Living Increase and Other Determinations for 2026", 90 FR 49047
--                                     (3 November 2025)
--   fr-2025-20251-cms-part-b-2026.txt CMS, Part B monthly actuarial rates, premium rate and deductible from 1 January 2026,
--                                     90 FR 52063 (19 November 2025)
-- as recorded in ../../registers/annual-figures.json. A question about any other year answers `not covered`: the 2027 notice
-- was not in the Federal Register on 2026-10-19 and earlier years' notices are not deposited.

§ `Figures set for each calendar year`

DECLARE `Annual figures` HAS
    -- s 415(a)(1)(B): the two bend points for those first eligible (or dying) in the year. 90 FR 49047: $1,286 and $7,749.
    `first PIA bend point`                         IS A NUMBER
    `second PIA bend point`                        IS A NUMBER
    -- s 403(a)(1)-(2): the three family maximum bend points. 90 FR 49047: $1,643, $2,371, $3,093.
    `first family maximum bend point`              IS A NUMBER
    `second family maximum bend point`             IS A NUMBER
    `third family maximum bend point`              IS A NUMBER
    -- s 413(d): the amount of wages and self-employment income for one quarter of coverage. 90 FR 49047: $1,890.
    `amount for a quarter of coverage`             IS A NUMBER
    -- s 403(f)(8): the monthly exempt amounts. 90 FR 49047: $2,040 ($24,480 a year) for a beneficiary under retirement age
    -- all year; $5,430 ($65,160 a year) in the year retirement age is reached.
    `lower monthly exempt amount`                  IS A NUMBER
    `higher monthly exempt amount`                 IS A NUMBER
    -- s 430: the contribution and benefit base. 90 FR 49047: $184,500.
    `contribution and benefit base`                IS A NUMBER
    -- s 415(i): the cost-of-living increase effective for December of the previous year. 90 FR 49047: 2.8 percent.
    `cost-of-living increase percent`              IS A NUMBER
    -- s 1382(b), s 1382f: the SSI federal benefit rate, monthly. 90 FR 49047: $994 (individual), $1,491 (couple).
    `SSI monthly rate for an individual`           IS A NUMBER
    `SSI monthly rate for an individual and eligible spouse` IS A NUMBER
    -- s 1382a(b)(1): the student earned income exclusion (the limit is the Commissioner's, set by 20 CFR 416.1112).
    -- 90 FR 49047: $2,410 a month, $9,730 a year.
    `SSI student earned income exclusion monthly`  IS A NUMBER
    `SSI student earned income exclusion yearly`   IS A NUMBER
    -- s 423(d)(4)(A): the earnings above which a blind individual may be regarded as able to engage in substantial gainful
    -- activity. 90 FR 49047: $2,830 a month.
    `substantial gainful activity amount, blind`   IS A NUMBER
    -- The SGA amount for non-blind individuals is set by regulation (20 CFR 404.1574), not by the Act. 90 FR 49047 publishes
    -- it: $1,690 a month. Carried as a published figure, marked ADMIN-POLICY wherever it is used.
    `substantial gainful activity amount, non-blind (regulation)` IS A NUMBER
    -- s 1395r(a)(3): the standard monthly Part B premium. 90 FR 52063: $202.90.
    `standard monthly Part B premium`              IS A NUMBER
    -- s 1395l(b): the Part B annual deductible. 90 FR 52063: $283.
    `Part B annual deductible`                     IS A NUMBER

`the 2026 figures` MEANS
    `Annual figures` WITH
        `first PIA bend point`                         IS 1286
        `second PIA bend point`                        IS 7749
        `first family maximum bend point`              IS 1643
        `second family maximum bend point`             IS 2371
        `third family maximum bend point`              IS 3093
        `amount for a quarter of coverage`             IS 1890
        `lower monthly exempt amount`                  IS 2040
        `higher monthly exempt amount`                 IS 5430
        `contribution and benefit base`                IS 184500
        `cost-of-living increase percent`              IS 2.8
        `SSI monthly rate for an individual`           IS 994
        `SSI monthly rate for an individual and eligible spouse` IS 1491
        `SSI student earned income exclusion monthly`  IS 2410
        `SSI student earned income exclusion yearly`   IS 9730
        `substantial gainful activity amount, blind`   IS 2830
        `substantial gainful activity amount, non-blind (regulation)` IS 1690
        `standard monthly Part B premium`              IS 202.90
        `Part B annual deductible`                     IS 283

-- The dated table: the figures in force for a calendar year, or NOTHING where no notice for that year is deposited.
GIVEN `calendar year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `Annual figures`
`the figures for` `calendar year` MEANS
    IF `calendar year` EQUALS 2026
        THEN JUST `the 2026 figures`
        ELSE NOTHING

-- Figures fixed in the Act itself, not indexed.
-- s 1382(a)(3)(B): the resource limit for an individual with no spouse with whom he is living, $2,000 from 1 January 1989.
`SSI resource limit for an individual` MEANS 2000
-- s 1382(a)(3)(A): for an individual with an eligible spouse, or living with a spouse, $3,000 from 1 January 1989.
`SSI resource limit for a couple` MEANS 3000
-- s 402(i): the lump-sum death payment is three times the PIA or $255, whichever is smaller.
`lump-sum death payment cap` MEANS 255
